Why: Win64 is LLP64.  The native-Win32 directory walker (USE_WIN32_FIND) 
stores the _findfirst() handle, an intptr_t, in a 'long', so it is 
truncated to 32 bits and _findnext()/_findclose() get a bogus handle.  
Effect on x86_64 MinGW: csant's <includes name="**/*.txt"/> filesets come 
back empty ('resgen: no inputs specified') or csant segfaults while 
building pnetlib.  Use intptr_t.  New patch (Win64 only; not in Guix).

diff --git a/support/dir.c b/support/dir.c
index 1285115..eb5c1b2 100644
--- a/support/dir.c
+++ b/support/dir.c
@@ -382,7 +382,7 @@ int ILDirEntType(ILDirEnt *entry)
 int ILGetFileType(const char *path)
 {
 	struct _finddata_t fileinfo;
-	long handle;
+	intptr_t handle;
 	handle = _findfirst(path, &fileinfo);
 	if(handle >= 0)
 	{
@@ -407,7 +407,7 @@ int ILGetFileType(const char *path)
  */
 struct _tagILDir
 {
-	long handle;
+	intptr_t handle;
 	struct _finddata_t fileinfo;
 	int havefirst;
 };
